# .dockerignore ─ exclude files not needed in any ASOE image
# NOTE: .python-version and uv.lock are intentionally NOT excluded —
# they are copied into images to pin Python 3.14 and lock dependencies.
.git
.gitignore
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
k8s/
infra/
docs/
.github/
.claude/

# Test tree handling.
#
# Dockerfile.api / Dockerfile.core never COPY anything under tests/,
# so excluding it shrinks their build context. Dockerfile.ui and
# Dockerfile.inference, however, intentionally COPY tests/sandbox/
# as application code:
#   * Dockerfile.ui     — Streamlit sandbox UI lives at
#                          tests/sandbox/ui/app.py.
#   * Dockerfile.inference — imports from tests/sandbox/llm/.
#
# A blanket `tests/` exclusion (the old rule) made those two
# Dockerfiles fail at COPY time with
# "/tests/sandbox": not found, so we instead exclude only the unit
# / sandbox test code and re-include the sandbox application
# subdirectories. Order matters: later rules win, so the runtime
# DB exclusions are placed last.
tests/**
!tests/__init__.py
!tests/sandbox
!tests/sandbox/**
tests/sandbox/sandbox.db
tests/sandbox/db/*.db

# Top-level markdown docs (skills/*_SKILL.md, prompts/*.md, and
# compliance/*.md are kept — they live inside dirs that are explicitly
# COPYed and are read at runtime).
/README.md
/CLAUDE.md
/DESIGN.md
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/architecture_v2.md
/architecture_v3.md
/tasks.md
/Login
